cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Blagden, please cite it as below."
title: "Blagden: heat intelligence for runners in the tropics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Panes
    given-names: Lawrence
    website: "https://lauurnce.is-a.dev"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-31
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lauurnce/blagden"
url: "https://blagden.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Blagden estimates core body temperature from run heart rate with the
  ECTemp extended Kalman filter, forecasts WBGT for a race venue from public
  forecast data, and produces a heat-adjusted finish-time prediction with a
  range. It ships as a Python library and CLI and an in-browser demo.
keywords:
  - running
  - heat stress
  - WBGT
  - core temperature
  - Kalman filter
  - sports science
  - Philippines
